  "title": "The Shared Tool’s Return Ticket",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "positive public good",
  "premise": "A community craft table wants to keep one hole punch available, but it vanishes under half-finished paper projects. A volunteer adds a bright outline where it belongs and a removable BORROWED card carried with it; the next borrower finds the card, waits visibly, and receives the returned tool without a search.",
  "hook": "The shared tool has entered the paper jungle.",
  "visible_action": "Paper piles spread; tool outline is drawn; BORROWED card travels with the punch; tool returns to its marked spot and card flips.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Make shared-resource status easy to see.",
  "gate": "Use a blunt toy craft tool; no assertion that this prevents theft or meets workplace safety requirements.",
